    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nMini.clue\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nIf I try to provide the `desc` for my keymapping inside of the setup function instead of at the time I create the keymapping, mini.clue will show the mapping as a viable path, but the place where it would show the description is empty.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.9.1\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nIn init.lua:\r\n1. create a mapping using `map` in vimL or `vim.keymap.set` in lua. do not provide the `desc`. \r\n2. setup mini.clue, provide the trigger for the keymap and add a `desc` in the clue for that mapping. \r\n\r\nIn new nvim instance:\r\n1. hit the initial trigger key. \r\n\r\nExample init.lua:\r\n```lua\r\n-- directly loading mini.nvim\r\nlocal minipath = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/lazy/mini.nvim\"\r\nvim.opt.rtp:prepend(minipath)\r\n\r\nvim.g.mapleader = ' '\r\nvim.cmd [[\r\n  nnoremap <Leader>b :buffers<CR>\r\n  nnoremap <Leader>l :help lsp \\| only<CR>\r\n]]\r\n\r\nrequire('mini.clue').setup({ -- Register `<Leader>` as trigger\r\n  triggers = {\r\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<Leader>' },\r\n    { mode = 'x', keys = '<Leader>' },\r\n  },\r\n\r\n  -- Add descriptions for mapping groups\r\n  clues = {\r\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<Leader>b', desc = '+Buffers' },\r\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<Leader>l', desc = '+LSP' },\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n..and then pressing `<Leader>` in a new instance will just show:\r\n![Screen Shot 2024-01-19 at 06 48 25](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/67888548/0877ea85-0471-4ef7-91e7-45c193ba3f61)\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nThe window showing the next possible keys should show a description for the options I mapped.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nThe window only shows the keybinding, but not the description. ",
