            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue.\r\n\r\nThis works [as expected](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/910e49d2d45e9d32c815d16cce6cea7c3b43cecf/doc/mini-clue.txt#L79-L82). The reason for this is for user to always be aware that there is a mapping behind certain clues. If user is not responsible for creating the mapping but still wants to show clue about it, there is a dedicated [`set_mapping_desc()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/910e49d2d45e9d32c815d16cce6cea7c3b43cecf/doc/mini-clue.txt#L623) to add description to existing mapping.",
